    <string name="moon_style_on_hour_hand">On the hour hand</string>
    <string name="moon_style_separate_hand">Own hand</string>
    <string name="moon_style_on_hour_hand_hint">The moon rides on the hour hand; its distance from the center shows its altitude. Where the path crosses the faint horizon circle, the moon rises or sets at that time.</string>
    <string name="moon_style_separate_hand_hint">The moon hand trails the hour hand by as much as the moon lags behind the sun, showing where the moon is in its daily course compared with the sun. Its distance from the center shows its altitude; the numerals do not give the times of moonrise and moonset.</string>
    <string name="show_next_alarm">Mark next alarm</string>
    <string name="next_alarm_hint">A red tick as soon as the next alarm falls within the displayed period. Android only reveals the next alarm to other apps, not all alarms that are set. When snoozing, the tick moves to the new alarm time if the clock app reports it.</string>

    <!-- Weather -->
    <string name="show_weather">Weather (clouds and precipitation)</string>
    <string name="weather_hint">Additional ring: gray depending on cloud cover, transparent when the sky is clear. Precipitation in blue (snow in violet): the darker, the more; the more opaque, the more likely. The forecast is downloaded about every two hours; for this, the place\'s coordinates are sent to open-meteo.com. %1$s.</string>
    <string name="weather_attribution">Weather data by Open-Meteo.com (CC BY 4.0)</string>
